# nexus-update sudoers entry — installed to /etc/sudoers.d/nexus-update
#
# Phase 9 (M_OTA). Grants the unprivileged `nexus` service user the
# narrow set of privileged commands an OTA apply needs, and ONLY
# those three exact commands, NOPASSWD (the engine runs unattended).
#
# Every command, argument, and path here MUST match byte-for-byte the
# `std::process::Command` invocations in
# `crates/nexus-engine/src/cloud_update.rs` (`install_release` +
# `flip_and_restart`). sudo matches the command line against these
# rules; any drift (a renamed path, an extra flag) makes the apply
# fail closed with a sudo password prompt that never gets answered.
#
# Scope rationale:
#   - `tar -xzf <staged> -C <releases>`: extract the verified tarball
#     (signature + sha256 already checked in-process by the engine
#     BEFORE this runs) into /opt/nexus/releases/<version>/.
#   - `ln -sfn /opt/nexus/releases/* /opt/nexus/current`: atomic flip
#     of the live symlink. The `*` wildcard covers the per-version
#     release dir; sudo's wildcard does NOT cross `/`, so this cannot
#     be coerced into linking an arbitrary tree outside releases/.
#   - `systemctl restart nexus-engine`: restart into the new version.
#     Pinned to the single unit; a compromised engine cannot pivot to
#     `systemctl` against any other unit, `apt`, etc.
#
# The bytes of the artifact never transit this boundary — the engine
# downloads + verifies them as the `nexus` user; sudo only touches
# already-staged, already-verified files.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g root deploy/sudoers.d/nexus-update \
#       /etc/sudoers.d/nexus-update
#   sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/nexus-update   # validate
nexus ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tar -xzf /opt/nexus/staging/update.tar.gz -C /opt/nexus/releases
nexus ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/ln -sfn /opt/nexus/releases/* /opt/nexus/current
nexus ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart nexus-engine
